Hey guys, I'm facing a similar problem with nested queries and percolator.

Just to be clear, this problem happens with any nested query, right? Because I have a simple percolate nested query that when executed against the index, it finds the document, but when used with the percolate query, no query is found for the document.

I'll leave my scenario here, so you guys can confirm it.

Elasticsearch version: 5.5.0
Docker Image: docker.elastic.co/elasticsearch/elasticsearch:5.5.0

Creating the index
```
PUT my_index
{
  "mappings": {
    "percolator": {
      "properties": {
        "query": {
          "type": "percolator"
        }
      }
    },
    "my_type": {
      "properties": {
        "tags": {
          "type": "nested",
          "properties": {
            "tag": {
              "type": "keyword"
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Adding a new document
```
POST my_index/my_type/1
{
  "tags": [
    {"tag": "first_tag"},
    {"tag": "second_tag"}
  ]
}
```

Testing the query we're gonna save in the percolator type
```
GET my_index/my_type/_search
{
  "query": {
    "nested": {
      "path": "tags",
      "query": {
        "bool": {
          "must": [
            {
              "match": {
                "tags.tag": "first_tag"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
The query works as expected.

Adding the query to the percolator type
```
PUT my_index/percolator/1?refresh
{
  "query": {
    "nested": {
      "path": "tags",
      "query": {
        "bool": {
          "must": [
            {
              "match": {
                "tags.tag": "first_tag"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Percolating the document
```
GET my_index/_search
{
  "query": {
    "percolate": {
      "field": "query",
      "document_type": "percolator",
      "document": {
        "tags": [
          {
            "tag": "first_tag"
          },
          {
            "tag": "second_tag"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
```
Here nothing is found!

I really hope to be doing something wrong, because for me this is a very important feature and my app depends on it.
